meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: World Population Prospects
    description: |-
      World Population Prospects 2024 is the 28th edition of the official estimates and projections of the global population that have been published by the United Nations since 1951. The estimates are based on all available sources of data on population size and levels of fertility, mortality and international migration for 237 countries or areas. If you have questions about this dataset, please refer to [their FAQ](https://population.un.org/wpp/faqs). You can also explore [data sources](https://population.un.org/wpp/data-sources) for each country or visit [their main page](https://population.un.org/wpp/) for more details.
    date_published: "2024-07-11"
    version_producer: "2024"
    title_snapshot: World Population Prospects - feed of the demography visualization
    description_snapshot: |-
      Our World in Data built this bundle of JSON files from World Population Prospects 2024 outside of the ETL, and published it by hand so that the "demography" bespoke visualization could fetch it. The bundle holds one file per entity, carrying that entity's population by age and sex, age-specific fertility rates, deaths by age and sex, net migration rate, and the same series for the projection scenarios, plus an index listing the entities and the file name of each.

      This snapshot captures those files exactly as they were being served, so that the feed can be published from the ETL without a byte of it changing. It is an interim measure: once the feed is built from the `un_wpp` garden dataset, this snapshot has no reason to exist.

    # Citation
    producer: United Nations
    citation_full: |-
      United Nations, Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population Division (2024). World Population Prospects 2024, Online Edition.
    attribution: UN, World Population Prospects (2024)
    attribution_short: UN WPP

    # Files
    url_main: https://population.un.org/wpp/downloads/
    date_accessed: "2026-09-17"

    # License
    license:
      name: CC BY 3.0 IGO
      url: https://population.un.org/wpp/downloads/
